          "domain": "information-and-ideas",
          "skill": "inferences",
          "passage": "When the microbial ecologist Colleen Cavanaugh and her colleagues began examining the giant tube worms that flourish around deep-sea hydrothermal vents, they noticed two features that did not fit the assumptions biologists had brought to the site. The worms have no mouth, no gut, and no obvious way to take in food, yet they thrive at densities far above those typical of the open ocean floor. Tissue samples revealed that a specialized organ inside each worm is densely packed with sulfur-oxidizing bacteria, which Cavanaugh's team showed could draw chemical energy from compounds vented through the cracks in the seafloor. Because the worms have no other apparent route to nutrition and the bacteria they host can build organic material from chemical energy alone, the team's combined findings suggest that ______",
