          "domain": "information-and-ideas",
          "skill": "inferences",
          "passage": "Working in lowland rain forests in the state of Veracruz, the tropical ecologist Rodolfo Dirzo has spent decades comparing forest plots that retain their full complement of large vertebrates with neighboring plots from which those animals have been hunted out. Two patterns recur across his sites. In plots without large mammals and birds, the seedlings of tree species with big seeds — which the missing animals would have carried away from the parent tree — fail at high rates and recruit poorly into mature size classes. Over the same intervals, the seedlings of tree species with smaller seeds, which can be moved by wind or by the small rodents and insects that remain, persist and reach maturity at rates indistinguishable from the unhunted plots. Because the patterns track seed size and the kinds of dispersers each size requires, Dirzo's combined findings suggest that ______",
