          "band": 2,
          "domain": "standard-english-conventions",
          "skill": "boundaries",
          "passage": "Anthropologist Margaret Mead spent more than two years on the Manus Islands of present-day Papua New Guinea before she returned to publish her 1930 ethnographic study of childhood in the region. The book did not stay confined to its specialist audience for ______ a wide American readership picked it up almost immediately, and parts of its argument quickly entered debates about American childhood that had little direct connection to the Manus communities Mead had visited.",
