          "type": "multiple-choice",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "band": 3,
          "domain": "standard-english-conventions",
          "skill": "form-structure-and-sense",
          "passage": "The geneticist Barbara McClintock spent the late 1940s and early 1950s carrying out her now-famous experiments on the variegated kernels of corn, painstakingly tracing the chromosomal rearrangements that produced their irregular color patterns. By the time the molecular structure of DNA was published by Watson and Crick in 1953, McClintock ______ the existence of mobile genetic elements in maize for several years, although that idea would not be widely accepted by other geneticists for decades.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?",
