          "skill": "words-in-context",
          "passage": "Molecular biologist Jennifer Doudna has spent much of the past decade thinking about how a research tool that began life as a bacterial defense system should be governed once it can be used to alter the DNA of plants, animals, and human embryos. According to her, the central question facing biologists is not whether the technology is technically possible — that is now beyond doubt — but how a community of researchers spread across many countries can ______ a shared set of rules for using it responsibly.",
