          "domain": "craft-and-structure",
          "skill": "words-in-context",
          "passage": "In her 2010 book *Art + Soul: A Journey into the World of Aboriginal Art*, the curator and writer Hetti Perkins argues that the dot paintings produced by senior Aboriginal Australian artists are too often misread by Western viewers as decorative regional ornament adapted to Western canvas. On Perkins's account, this framing fails to register what the paintings actually are. A given canvas, she suggests, may simultaneously hold information meant for the wider public and information ______ Country-specific knowledge whose meaning is reserved for those with the appropriate ceremonial standing within the artist's community.",
