          "band": 4,
          "domain": "standard-english-conventions",
          "skill": "boundaries",
          "passage": "In their 2012 essay \"Decolonization Is Not a Metaphor,\" the education researchers Eve Tuck and K. Wayne Yang argue that calls to \"decolonize\" classrooms, syllabi, and academic disciplines have become so routine that the word risks losing its political meaning. They are not opposed to those reforms ______ they argue that decolonization, in any substantive sense, requires the actual return of land and sovereignty to Indigenous peoples, and that work cannot be substituted by classroom changes alone, however well intentioned.",
